<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William I of the Netherlands</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1772">1772</a>–<a href="/years/1843">1843</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as King William I of the Netherlands</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William I was the first King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, reigning from 1815 to 1840. A son of William V, the last stadtholder, and great-grandson of William IV of Orange-Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diez">Diez</a>, he ruled the United Kingdom of the Netherlands, including present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. He promoted trade, canals and industry, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgian-revolution">Belgian Revolution</a> of 1830 split his kingdom, and he abdicated in 1840.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-i-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="William I of the Netherlands" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Paelinck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_I_of_the_Netherlands.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
